[{"sha":"1927658ad6a97788bd86fc59310d1ed45a08e60e","node_id":"C_kwDOBEmZvdoAKDE5Mjc2NThhZDZhOTc3ODhiZDg2ZmM1OTMxMGQxZWQ0NWEwOGU2MGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"MatthewCWeston","email":"61944935+MatthewCWeston@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-05-27T10:20:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-27T10:20:35Z"},"message":"Fix two substantial edge cases in PPO's value target calculation (#59958)\n\n## Description\n`AddOneTsToEpisodesAndTruncate` currently has two edge cases which cause\nsignificant errors in value target calculation.\n\n* The first is that, when lambda is set to zero *(pure value\nbootstrapping)*, terminal rewards are discarded from value target\ncalculation for earlier states. This is because a terminated flag is\nplaced in the second-to-last timestep of the modified episodes,\nresulting in said rewards being masked out.\n* In effect, this means that, in an environment with terminal rewards,\nwe only learn a policy for the very last timestep!\n\n* The second is that truncated episodes do not make use of value head\ncalculations from the last observation, under the same conditions. This\nis because the terminated flag is appended to every episode, regardless\nof whether the episode actually terminates.\n* In effect, this means that truncation is treated identically to\ntermination, except that the bug described in the prior bullet point\ndoes not occur, and value targets fail to include any of the potential\nfuture rewards after the truncation point.\n\nThis PR fixes both issues and includes a pair of unit tests to prevent\nregression. One is a lightweight test of an environment whose state\nvalues can be quickly learned, which checks for both correct learning\nand plausible state values. The other directly evaluates the correctness\nof value target calculations on a toy dataset.\n\n[This Colab\nnotebook](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24485996/scratch_for_value_bootstrapping_fix.ipynb)\nallows both of the above bugs to be readily verified. The topmost cell\nwill patch in the fix from this PR. Run it before the below cells to\ntest the fix. Skip running it altogether to test the code that is\ncurrently in production.\n\n## Related issues\nResolves the bug outlined in\nhttps://github.com/ray-project/ray/issues/57683.\n\nResolves the additional issue raised in #57895.\n\n## Additional information\n\nA prior PR submitted by me failed to address the second edge case, and\nwas closed as a result. This PR should correctly resolve both of them.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Matthew <mweston3@illinois.edu>\nSigned-off-by: Artur Niederfahrenhorst <artur@anyscale.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mark Towers <mark.m.towers@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Artur Niederfahrenhorst <artur@anyscale.com>","tree":{"sha":"ac814cf46d0e16cb2a798f23cf430b20ebb44e4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ray-project/ray/git/trees/ac814cf46d0e16cb2a798f23cf430b20ebb44e4f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ray-project/ray/git/commits/1927658ad6a97788bd86fc59310d1ed45a08e60e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqFsVzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFa4QABGPSvj03B7CPR73fhZU4ExC\njvme4zS8MTCyURj/Wziz+V9Zvz0UbroHPM0io9/Dq4d384CttHMYUO/4OjtHGpx5\nuFi2QC0bgaBOtfrlVjrK9CPFO1I6dDrWkqKo0nfK/zfA6S+m6xd8x2ed3TRhGLyE\nR6USSvxMhr4gjfTuqzbJqgVrhQcYWFqJ/V0AwriCyrG+MsFoLm4kwwcTN+dUWqFz\nfQRnjM9m8gjujBoAwJgDgGvq+QzBV+Sv03r2XDu/M9ocGDki554m0K2/ByYzis9E\nDq/D0/snTgp/aIKTmv4HaBjW3llpddi4U9WZfBWs3adeo8kgKD91Y4zCB4NiHopQ\n1El5DdGa1OsZI75rfPRnET9UCK/EdQci0QpHJ851YTJi7AlVlGzGvIaC4V3t10Ro\nGp4jWaJPhL8FAgvaoqwy0ouBADMLh8wK0K+RRHVrMu9SXxKBMsClEdLACaf+k8n1\n/nxpsb4B+ju7aOW3q4FKO200TH11HMdhjvZGEIyW16f1HFL1Li/EZFS6x50fTeoW\nLgArxRVCBhDkDJ1Scc4w26H0CXyUVtsn+uZFmSmu62R27MWuzjJFwOoDJdydsLPR\nC5Dh3gpzJDCKsEdvdd1AxcSouidEuBJJnMh2hbROO+OCntGFkCdU5eouIkqA4WDA\nSgF0V4QK44JwylGIT8su\n=vWXZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ac814cf46d0e16cb2a798f23cf430b20ebb44e4f\nparent ba235570696d1525e74534be213d8d1a168ae28a\nauthor MatthewCWeston <61944935+MatthewCWeston@users.noreply.github.com> 1779877235 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779877235 +0000\n\nFix two substantial edge cases in PPO's value target calculation (#59958)\n\n## Description\n`AddOneTsToEpisodesAndTruncate` currently has two edge cases which cause\nsignificant errors in value target calculation.\n\n* The first is that, when lambda is set to zero *(pure value\nbootstrapping)*, terminal rewards are discarded from value target\ncalculation for earlier states. This is because a terminated flag is\nplaced in the second-to-last timestep of the modified episodes,\nresulting in said rewards being masked out.\n* In effect, this means that, in an environment with terminal rewards,\nwe only learn a policy for the very last timestep!\n\n* The second is that truncated episodes do not make use of value head\ncalculations from the last observation, under the same conditions. This\nis because the terminated flag is appended to every episode, regardless\nof whether the episode actually terminates.\n* In effect, this means that truncation is treated identically to\ntermination, except that the bug described in the prior bullet point\ndoes not occur, and value targets fail to include any of the potential\nfuture rewards after the truncation point.\n\nThis PR fixes both issues and includes a pair of unit tests to prevent\nregression. One is a lightweight test of an environment whose state\nvalues can be quickly learned, which checks for both correct learning\nand plausible state values. The other directly evaluates the correctness\nof value target calculations on a toy dataset.\n\n[This Colab\nnotebook](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24485996/scratch_for_value_bootstrapping_fix.ipynb)\nallows both of the above bugs to be readily verified. The topmost cell\nwill patch in the fix from this PR. Run it before the below cells to\ntest the fix. Skip running it altogether to test the code that is\ncurrently in production.\n\n## Related issues\nResolves the bug outlined in\nhttps://github.com/ray-project/ray/issues/57683.\n\nResolves the additional issue raised in #57895.\n\n## Additional information\n\nA prior PR submitted by me failed to address the second edge case, and\nwas closed as a result. This PR should correctly resolve both of them.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Matthew <mweston3@illinois.edu>\nSigned-off-by: Artur Niederfahrenhorst <artur@anyscale.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mark Towers <mark.m.towers@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Artur Niederfahrenhorst <artur@anyscale.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-27T10:20:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ray-project/ray/commits/1927658ad6a97788bd86fc59310d1ed45a08e60e","html_url":"https://github.com/ray-project/ray/commit/1927658ad6a97788bd86fc59310d1ed45a08e60e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ray-project/ray/commits/1927658ad6a97788bd86fc59310d1ed45a08e60e/comments","author":{"login":"MatthewCWeston","id":61944935,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTQ0OTM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61944935?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthewCWeston","html_url":"https://github.com/MatthewCWeston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthewCWeston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthewCWeston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthewCWeston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthewCWeston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthewCWeston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthewCWeston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthewCWeston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthewCWeston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthewCWeston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","sit